Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 13:51:02 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10786/11171] One of the four shipped-but-unevaluated flags is
 inert, not pending

CARNOT_ARC_INDUCE_CANDIDATE_TOOLS cannot be evaluated. register_candidate_tool
exists and arc_tool_gap_refinement documents it as the human-authored path, but it
has zero non-test callers. Nothing is registered, so enabling the flag changes
nothing and no A/B of it can produce a result. Found by the follow-up agent while
staging the tool A/B; verified here by grepping callers.

The reason to record it is the counter, which is mine. The outer-loop dashboard has
printed 4/4 shipped-but-unevaluated every hour this session, reading as four
capabilities awaiting measurement. Three are. The fourth is awaiting an AUTHOR, and
a counter that renders "never evaluated" and "cannot be evaluated" identically will
keep someone queueing an experiment with no possible outcome.

This is the AVO boundary appearing as a gap rather than a bug: tool proposal is
human work, a 27B local model selects over a curated set and cannot author the tool,
so an empty registry is the expected state until someone writes one. The defect is
that nothing says so where the flag is counted.

Cheap fix recorded and not built: have the dashboard check whether the registry is
non-empty and label the flag inert rather than unevaluated. Read-only, contained to
scripts/outer_loop_dashboard.py.

